---
// src/pages/about.astro
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Skills from '../components/Skills.astro';
import Capabilities from '../components/Capabilities.astro';
import VideoGallery from '../components/VideoGallery.astro';
import MusicTaste from '../components/MusicTaste.astro';
import AvatarCard from '../components/AvatarCard.astro';

const projects = await getCollection('projects');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const notes = [
  {
    n: '01',
    h: 'What I build',
    body: `I learn fastest when I have something real to make. That has led me through Discord platforms with authentication and payments, Rust and Tauri desktop apps, SaaS backends, and security tools. There are ${projects.length} projects here, and each description is checked against the code or notes I still have.`,
    link: { href: `${base}projects/`, label: 'See my projects' },
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    h: 'How I got here',
    body: `I manage an EHCP (Education, Health and Care Plan) alongside my studies. It has pushed me to be deliberate about how I work: break a problem down, keep notes while I go and finish one part properly before moving on.`,
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    h: "What I'm looking for",
    body: `I'm looking for a paid cybersecurity or IT apprenticeship, or a junior technical role. I want somewhere I can contribute what I already know, learn from experienced people and keep improving through practical work.`,
    link: { href: `${base}credentials/`, label: 'See my security practice' },
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    h: 'Right now',
    body: `Right now I'm building KUSH, my software and digital-services business. I handle its website, backend, Discord server and bot; it is still being prepared for launch. I'm also Chief Security Officer at Velnqo, a hosting and infrastructure business that is being set up.`,
    link: { href: `${base}projects/kush/`, label: 'KUSH case study' },
  },
];
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Oscar Senior (Nops): final-year cybersecurity and IT student at DISC, founder of KUSH and Chief Security Officer at Velnqo. In his own words.">
  <PageIntro
    index="05"
    label="Personal"
    title="About"
    accent="me."
    film={{
      name: 'about-deck',
      title: 'Deck',
      fig: 'Fig. 06',
      caption: 'Deck. A turntable under red and magenta light, because music is the one thing on this page I call non-negotiable.',
      alt: 'A turntable with a spinning black record and a metal tonearm, lit in red and magenta.',
    }}
  >
    <p>I'm a final-year student at DISC, specialising in cybersecurity and IT, and I'm looking for a paid cybersecurity apprenticeship, IT apprenticeship, or junior technical role.</p>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="sec notes wrap" data-scene="page">
    {
      notes.map((note, i) => (
        <article class="note" data-reveal={i > 0 ? '' : undefined}>
          <span class="note-n">{note.n}</span>
          <div class="note-body">
            <h2>{note.h}</h2>
            <p>{note.body}</p>
            {note.link && (
              <a href={note.link.href} class="link-arrow">
                {note.link.label}
                <span class="arr">→</span>
              </a>
            )}
          </div>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap personal-sec" data-scene="stack">
    <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="sec-index">05</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-split data-reveal>Off the clock</h2>
      </div>
      <span class="meta">Not the CV version</span>
      <span class="sec-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="personal-grid">
      <AvatarCard />
    <div class="personal-copy" data-reveal>
        <p>I'm Nops. Nineteen, mostly running on curiosity and a fairly stubborn need to know how things actually work under the hood.</p>
        <p>If something catches my attention, that's kind of it for me — I'll pull it apart, read too much about it at 1am, break it, fix it, and only really relax once I understand it properly rather than just knowing it works. I don't do "good enough" very well. If I can't see the reasoning behind something, I'll poke at it until I can, and I'd rather figure something out badly on my own than be handed the answer.</p>
        <p>Most of that energy goes toward computers, Linux, security, and building things — but it's not really about the subject, it's the process. Give me a system and I want to know its edges: what breaks it, what it wasn't designed for, what happens if you do the thing you're not supposed to do. Outside of screens, it's motorcycles (a Hayabusa is the one that lives rent-free in my head), hockey, anime, and going places that actually feel like somewhere rather than a checklist. Snake Pass in the Peak District is the kind of place I mean — I'll take character over a postcard view every time. Sweden's high on the list too, partly for the place, partly because I've got a friend out there.</p>
        <p>Music is non-negotiable. Alternative, emo, metal, post-hardcore — Avenged Sevenfold, Deftones, Slipknot, My Chemical Romance, Silverstein, that whole world, but I'll happily swing into Paramore or HIM or $uicideboy$ depending on what kind of day it is. Some of it's just good, some of it's tied to specific memories I'm weirdly protective of. My taste in general leans dark and a bit stripped back — black, charcoal, red and magenta lighting, not much clutter. I like spaces and things that feel like mine, not something screenshotted off Pinterest.</p>
        <p>My sense of humour is probably the most "me" thing about me, and it's a bit unhinged. I find an unreasonable amount of joy in ideas that are completely pointless but committed — the kind of thing where someone asks a normal question and I answer it in the most technically-correct, least-intended way possible. Ask me to bring back a band for one final show and I'm not booking a venue, I'm teleporting them into my bedroom. I enjoy that gap between what a question means and what it actually says, and I live in it more than is probably healthy. I'll also just go along with a stupid idea way further than it deserves, purely because stopping would be boring.</p>
        <p>I'm not one thing consistently, either. I can go quiet for a while and then not shut up the second you get me on something I care about. I get excited fast and fully, I'm sentimental about specific small stuff — Camp Bestival as a kid, push-up ice creams, songs that pull me straight back to a moment — even if I don't always say that out loud. I care a lot about the people I let in, more than I probably show day to day.</p>
        <p>I'm not trying to be the most impressive person you've read about today. I just like understanding things, laughing at ideas that don't need to exist, and building stuff because I want to see if I can. That's genuinely most of it — the rest of this site is what I've made. This part's just me.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="inspired">
      <div class="inspired-head" data-reveal>
        <h3>Inspired by</h3>
        <p>Clips from other creators that I'm into — none of these are mine. Each one is credited to the person who made it.</p>
        <p class="meta">Sound is off until you turn it on</p>
      </div>
      <VideoGallery />
    </div>

    <MusicTaste />
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap">
    <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="sec-index">06</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-split data-reveal>Technical capabilities</h2>
      </div>
      <span class="meta">Drawn from the projects on this site</span>
      <span class="sec-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <Capabilities />
  </section>

  <section class="sec wrap">
    <div class="sec-head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="sec-index">07</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-split data-reveal>Skills breakdown</h2>
      </div>
      <span class="meta">Calculated from {projects.length} project records</span>
      <span class="sec-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <Skills />
  </section>

  <section class="sec contact-sec wrap" data-scene="contact" data-reveal>
    <div class="contact-inner glass" data-glass>
      <div>
        <p class="sec-index">08</p>
        <h2 class="sec-title" data-split data-reveal>Contact</h2>
        <p class="cta-line">Hiring an apprentice or junior developer? <a href="mailto:nopsrust@gmail.com">Email me</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="contact-list">
        <li><span>Email</span> <a href="mailto:nopsrust@gmail.com">nopsrust@gmail.com</a></li>
        <li><span>GitHub</span> <a href="https://github.com/Oscar1-dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/Oscar1-dev</a></li>
        <li><span>TryHackMe</span> <a href="https://tryhackme.com/p/Oscar.Senior" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tryhackme.com/p/Oscar.Senior</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .notes {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 88px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .note:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .note-n {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--page-accent);
    text-shadow: 0 0 1px var(--color-bg), 0 1px 4px var(--color-bg), 0 0 14px var(--color-bg);
  }

  .note-body {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .note-body h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  .note-body p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .note {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
  }

  .personal-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 340px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .personal-grid :global(.me) {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) + 24px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .personal-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .personal-grid :global(.me) {
      position: static;
    }
  }
  .personal-copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .personal-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .personal-copy p:first-child {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .inspired {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .inspired-head {
    margin-bottom: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem);
  }

  .inspired-head h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .inspired-head p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 58ch;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .inspired-head .meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .contact-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(240px, 0.9fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: start;
    padding: clamp(22px, 3.5vw, 44px);
  }

  .cta-line {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .cta-line a {
    text-shadow: 0 0 1px var(--color-bg), 0 1px 4px var(--color-bg), 0 0 14px var(--color-bg);
  }

  .contact-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: var(--space-6);
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    background: var(--color-bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
  }

  .contact-list li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .contact-list span {
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .contact-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
